id: pm-slack-standup-7t31
title: Require exact all-source 100/100/100/100 coverage and strict quality gates
description: "The current V8 coverage gate measures only index.ts at 90.44% lines, 88.23% branches, and 91.79% functions, with no separately reported statements result. release:check now enforces canonical pm-ops ESLint lint and zero-duplication checks plus the docstring gate, but executable scripts remain outside coverage and the mutation and broader static/security gate criteria remain incomplete. This blocks an all-source 100/100/100/100 or production-ready claim."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: coverage,quality-gate,release-blocker,tdd
created_at: "2026-08-21T10:11:53.131Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-04T22:56:57.186Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "Inventory every executable TypeScript and JavaScript source; replace or explicitly justify JavaScript; measure statements, branches, functions, and lines across every executable source at exact 100 percent; make the gate fail when a source is added or removed from measurement; add strict lint, duplication and security/static gates with no blanket suppression; mutation-check the gate; keep tests behavior-driven and non-duplicative"
definition_of_ready: Current release gate and source inventory are measured on main.
reviewer: greptile
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-08-quality
release: future
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: "main 2d0077a, Node V8 coverage"
repro_steps: Run npm run coverage and inspect coverage-gate DEFAULT_SKIP_DIRS plus package thresholds.
expected_result: All executable repository source is measured at exact 100/100/100/100 and every strict quality gate is mandatory.
actual_result: "All-source coverage gate: 238 tests pass; 11 authored sources (operational scripts included, no ignores) at 100/100/100/100; thresholds must be exactly 100; docstring 89 declarations; duplication 0%; release:check passes on the PR #107 head."
affected_version: pm-slack-standup 2026.8.17
component: quality and release gates
customer_impact: "A green release gate can coexist with untested source and below-mandate coverage, so it cannot support a production-ready claim."
comments[23]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-22T05:10:25.678Z",pi-agent,"Not closed by the 2026.9.21 certify task pm-slack-standup-add0. That task delivers the canonical pm-ops lint and duplication gates only. This item still requires exact 100/100/100/100 all-source coverage, mutation checking, and the broader security/static analyzers named in its acceptance criteria."
  "2026-10-02T21:14:35.906Z",pi-grok,"Current-state actual_result now reports the later 21:38 certification run of 207/207. The 206-test result remains in the append-only history event from 2026-09-28T21:23:29.863Z. Later commits after that run do not add tests."
  "2026-10-03T00:00:48.172Z",codex-sol,"npm ci and npm run release:check PASS: 207/207 tests, zero skipped; measured index.ts coverage 90.44/88.23/91.79 lines/branches/functions with unchanged 83/87/87 floors; 81 documented declarations. Independent statements, whole-source 100 percent, mutation and broader static/security acceptance remain unmeasured/unaccepted in pm-slack-standup-7t31. Canonical-reader acceptance and all five packed npm/Bun current/minimum/global scenarios pass. Audit all/production zero; strict CI health, pm validate, Bun install and CI fresh-dist comparison pass. Linked packaging tests pass 2/2 and focused PATH fallback test 1/1 passes after failing red on a populated temporary ancestor. The fixture now owns all four searched directories and a shim just outside the bound, preserving real fallback assertions without touching other workspaces. Retained 207 count correction and original 206 history event preserved; all JSONL prefixes unchanged. Note projections support edit/delete in pinned CLI; immutable history is retained. Final-head CI and substantive reviews remain separate; both items released in_progress, never closed."
  "2026-10-04T08:50:03.993Z",pi-glm,"cubic-dev-ai finding (PR 97 third round): the description still labeled the superseded 88.38 percent branch figure as current while actual_result reports 88.23. Fixed through the pm CLI in 923e16c: the description's current coverage baseline now states the measured 90.44/88.23/91.79 lines/branches/functions. Historical receipts in the immutable JSONL history are unchanged; the projection edit is appended as a new history event. Full gate re-validated at 923e16c: npm ci and npm run release:check PASS — 207/207 tests, zero skipped; measured index.ts coverage exactly 90.44/88.23/91.79 with unchanged 83/87/87 floors; 81 documented declarations; lint, duplication, canonical-reader, audit:prod, pack, all five packed npm/Bun scenarios, changelog:check, release-changelog-date and publish-attestation green. Independent statements, whole-source 100 percent, mutation and broader static/security acceptance remain unmeasured/unaccepted here."
  "2026-10-04T08:58:54.454Z",pi-glm,"Correction to the previous verification note: the cited 923e16c was amended before it was ever pushed, so it does not resolve in the repository. The coverage-baseline correction and the full release gate evidence are verified at the pushed commit 96d14c3 (npm ci and npm run release:check PASS, 207/207 tests, measured index.ts coverage 90.44/88.23/91.79 with unchanged 83/87/87 floors; linked pm test npm run coverage passes with the same numbers). The original note with the stale reference remains in the immutable history events; this note is the current, verifiable receipt."
  "2026-10-04T11:30:51.838Z",codex-sol,"Certification pm-slack-standup-74w8 preserves thresholds (83 lines/87 branches/87 functions). Existing recorded scope is index.ts only: 90.44% lines/88.23% branches/91.79% functions; scripts excluded by existing source inventory and independent statements unmeasured. This is a substantial coverage gap rather than a small fixture-only closure, so certification will record the fresh result here and will not claim 100/100/100/100 or lower any gate."
  "2026-10-04T11:42:58.673Z",codex-sol,"Fresh certification measurement confirms the existing coverage gap exactly: 90.44/88.23/91.79, 207/207 tests, zero skipped, 1 source index.ts. Canonical lint and duplication PASS (0% of 8775 lines; 26 sources). Remaining script and independent statement coverage are outside this compatibility refresh and remain required here; no threshold reduction or new ignore."
  "2026-10-04T17:45:22.135Z",codex-sol,"Coverage work on test/cover-every-standup-path: measure every authored runtime TypeScript source including scripts; add separately measured statements and retain source presence checks. Behavioral tests and real disposable PM projects; no coverage ignores or mocked module under test. Runtime coverage delegated to isolated Codex CLI agent under current quota policy."
  "2026-10-04T17:52:27.353Z",codex-sol,"Gate regression first failed against the old implementation (missing runGate/collectSources exports). New gate measures statements independently with c8 12.0.0, inventories operational scripts, verifies type-only erasure with native Node stripping, isolates config/counters, removes stale LCOV before and after failure, and reconciles report filenames. Seven real child-suite fixtures pass; focused coverage-gate.ts coverage is exactly 100 statements/branches/functions/lines. Reproduced and fixed inherited NODE_TEST_CONTEXT causing recursive child suite suppression. No source behavior removed."
  "2026-10-04T17:57:08.366Z",codex-sol,"Orchestrator verification: full baseline release gate reaches 215 passing tests with zero skips; all-source measurement is 85.19 statements/lines, 89.61 branches, 90.24 functions, correctly fails 100 thresholds. Fixed a race in the source-disappearance regression by deleting the loaded source inside one test rather than two concurrent files. Manual packed README preview and Markdown export render four real disposable PM items with all four sections. Production audit clean, changelog remains up to date."
  "2026-10-04T17:59:34.003Z",codex-sol,"Hardened both report receipts: failures invalidate coverage-summary.json as well as LCOV. Hostile .c8rc configuration cannot narrow the package-owned inventory. Focused gate remains measured 100/100/100/100; lint, duplication 0%, and test compilation pass."
  "2026-10-04T18:16:59.099Z",codex-sol,"Integration verified against source commits 09fa83763956c6fdaee3694cbb542b751f4988a5 (runtime) and 45e68dbfce46575ce3d245affa358b4adea991be (tooling). The conservative history union refused one redundant remove after concurrent collection edits, and receipt reconciliation could not prove the candidate. Aborted that tracker union, restored the exact verified original item and history, and archived the original worker histories plus hash-only failed receipt as evidence. No history events discarded or forced repair; original worker streams remain intact in docs/evidence. Record integrated code/tests/docs here through normal audited mutations. Runtime worker measured 155 passing tests and all four metrics 100; tooling worker measured nine scripts at all four metrics 100 with 58 passing tests. Combined pinned 2026.10.4 gates still to run."
  "2026-10-04T18:24:14.640Z",codex-sol,"Orchestrator combined verification passed npm run release:check exit 0 against pinned installed CLI/SDK 2026.10.4 on Node 24.19.0: 241 tests, zero failures/skips; all 11 authored runtime TypeScript files 100/100/100/100, 4002/4002 lines/statements, 1066/1066 branches, 130/130 functions. Typecheck/lint/build/test compilation, docstrings 11 files/90 declarations, duplication 0% across 36 sources, production audit 0 vulnerabilities, canonical reader, dry-run packing, five packed npm/Bun host scenarios, unchanged changelog, calendar date and provenance gates passed. Erasable syntax compile passed and is now enforced in tsconfig. Fresh final packed manual README preview/export shows four real initialized PM fixtures in all four sections. Worker history streams preserved intact; active item history verifies with no mismatches. Coverage evidence docs/all-source-coverage.md. Final committed-head linked gate to follow."
  "2026-10-04T18:33:08.710Z",codex-sol,"Final committed-head verification retained exact 100% across all 11 source files; 240 tests passed and the per-commit identity/privacy test rejected an absolute host path in a pasted changelog receipt. Removed that path from the unpublished commit without weakening the audit. Changelog success remains recorded as a result, while published pass lines contain no host-home paths. Rerunning the final committed-head full gate using supported tracker/source context; no test or threshold weakened."
  "2026-10-04T18:44:29.749Z",codex-sol,"Opened PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/107 after final committed-head linked release:check passed 241 tests, zero skips and all 11 sources 100/100/100/100. Remote matched tested commit 1cdaefb71418ac587639eb441cf30148cc39dbb2; tracker history verified 40 entries with no mismatch. Initial CodeQL annotation flagged incomplete escaping in a test regex constructed solely from four constant labels. Replace it with an equivalent literal includes assertion, preserving the exact observable labels and avoiding unnecessary regex construction. Existing Windows shell-launch annotation remains tracked by pm-slack-standup-z1up; no portable behavior removed. CI and substantive reviews remain pending; skipped/quota-limited reviews are not approvals."
  "2026-10-04T18:58:37.469Z",codex-sol,"PR #107 review round: reproduce fixture escaping and npm_execpath fallback findings with failing tests first, then repair and rerun release:check at unchanged 100/100/100/100 coverage thresholds."
  "2026-10-04T19:03:03.481Z",codex-sol,"Red test observed: packed acceptance with npm_execpath unset under a copied Node executable failed before packing because the test invented a nonexistent npm entry. Preserve the inherited environment and exercise inherited and unset cases. Finding 4178833812 was already fixed by commit 8217431: literal includes replaces incomplete regex escaping."
  "2026-10-04T19:10:34.810Z",codex-sol,"Additional red test: unset npm_execpath on Windows selected npm.cmd, which cannot be launched through the shell-free runner. acceptanceLaunchers now resolves the real npm and npx JavaScript entries from an explicit PATH in npm prefix layouts. A portable fixture test runs both entries as real child processes and verifies literal arguments. The pinned npm_execpath retains precedence."
  "2026-10-04T19:16:32.902Z",codex-sol,"Final tracker-linked npm run release:check passed with exit code 0: 235 tests, zero failed/skipped; all 11 executable source files at 100/100/100/100 with no ignores; duplication 0 percent (0/8918), 36 sources and no clone pairs; 89 documented declarations; zero production vulnerabilities. Both inherited/unset npm_execpath packed matrices and the separate five-scenario packed gate passed. Typecheck, lint, build, canonical reader, changelog consistency, release-date and publish-attestation gates passed. Erasable syntax, tracker health/validation and diff checks passed. Changelog regeneration was unnecessary. See docs/review-107.md. Remote Windows execution and new CodeQL scan remain pending after push."
  "2026-10-04T21:48:48.887Z",codex-sol,"PR #107: read all seven CodeRabbit findings. Plan real-directory PM/npm launcher regressions and a symlink-root coverage reproduction before fixes, retain warmed-up absolute argv validation ceiling, remove generated file links, and refresh evidence counts from the final release:check."
  "2026-10-04T21:51:17.628Z",codex-sol,"Red regressions observed: Windows npm configuration and missing npm/npx pair returned unsupported shims instead of throwing; symlink-root run reached 100 percent then rejected its real-path inventory; bare PM layout test executed both real entries but refusal omitted PM_BIN. Fixed canonical root usage and complete PATH pair selection. Removed warmed-up argv timing ratio; retained 5000 ms median ceiling. pm get --full confirms all generated dist links are gone."
  "2026-10-04T21:57:22.440Z",codex-sol,"Verified tracker-linked npm run release:check passed with exit 0: 238 tests, zero failed/skipped; all 11 authored executable sources at 100/100/100/100; duplication 0 percent (0/9005), 36 sources, zero clone pairs; 89 documented declarations; zero production vulnerabilities. Canonical reader, packed five-scenario npm/Bun gate, pack dry run, changelog consistency, release-date and publish-attestation checks passed. No ignores or threshold reductions. Refreshed final-tree documentation and marked earlier focused receipts historical. Final committed-head gate will run before push; Windows execution and remote review remain separate evidence."
  "2026-10-04T22:56:57.186Z",claude-orchestrator,"Review (CodeRabbit, PR #107): the coverage gate now refuses any configured threshold other than exactly 100 (adversarial cases 0 and 99.99 added; the test failed before the change), and actual_result reflects the final 238-test receipt."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
